    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0741" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115C96/114</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Hostetter to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Hermosillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-01T11:00:00-07:23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1916, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s February 24, 6 p.m. Obregon just arrived and spoke to him about
                    Chihuahua district. Says he has sent additional troops with very good generals,
                    Herrera and Gutiérres, who thoroughly know country, with orders to push pursuit
                    and earnestly hopes to have district cleared very soon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hostetter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
